WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.666
- We did it! This city means the world to me. Tampa forever!

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:06.375
All right, only 30 more teams to go. Gronk, we're out.

00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:08.125
- But Gronk just bought a house.

00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:08.875
- Just buy another one—

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:11.791
- [Jared Goff:] Look at this guy. A Super Bowl-winning quarterback.

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:16.166
Me? I lost a Super Bowl, and two years later, they shipped me off to Detroit with this guy—

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:19.250
- WOO! WELCOME TO THE LION CAGE! HAVE DINNER OR BECOME DINNER!

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:20.875
- [Goff:] They traded Stafford to L.A.—

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:21.875
- OH GOD, THE SUN.

00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:24.000
- [Goff:] For me, a third and two firsts.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.625
- Oh! Gotta tip. Here’s our 2024 first-round pick.

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.250
- [Goff:] Suddenly, the price for a QB increased even more,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.375
which gave one man an idea...

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:34.666
- TAYSOM…we’re gonna drive up the price of quarterback stock.

00:00:37.541 --> 00:00:42.250
Hello, media, can I interest you in Taysom Hill?
He’s Mormon but also old.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.875
- [Media on phone:] Well, gosh, I don’t know—

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:45.875
- TAYSOM COULD PUNT AND RETURN THE SAME KICK.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.125
- Well, all right! Taysom to the moon, baby! Lock me in!

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:49.125
- I got you, no cap.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:52.291
- [Goff:] Confusing? Here’s Adam Lefkoe in a bathtub to explain.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.375
- The Saints are $100 million over the salary cap already, and

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:58.500
this year, the cap is actually going to get LOWER for the first time in a decade.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.041
So the Saints need to increase Taysom’s trade value.

00:01:01.666 --> 00:01:03.125
You guys are going to make me look good, right?

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:06.041
- So Taysom is now worth $40 million a year? Hmmm.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.750
- So, is the exit interview over?

00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:10.791
- THEY ARE MAKING MORE MONEY THAN ME.
WE NEED TO IMPOSE RESTRICTIONS.

00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:11.666
- Maybe Taysom is good?

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:13.791
- NO, EVERYTHING IS ABOUT MON—

00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:16.750
- Great season, Team State Farm!
[car horn, honking]

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.916
Yeah, honk for State Farm!

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:23.000
- MONEY, EVERYTHING.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.375
- [Goff:] So with Taysom rising, the price on more experienced QBs went through the roof.

00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:30.291
- Dang it, Dakky. I gotta sell my Jumbotron to pay ya!

00:01:30.291 --> 00:01:32.625
- This is why you should have extended me earlier, Jerral.

00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:36.666
- Used car! Selling a lightly used car, man. I mean, this baby still drives, man.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.916
- Look, the internet says now I’m worth half a Darnoldcoin.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.500
- TAYSOM, WATCH ME DANCE.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.750
- [Taysom Hill:] Uh, Coach. You should trade me—

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.625
- HOLD THE LINE.

00:01:44.166 --> 00:01:46.750
- Sorry, Deshaun. If Taysom Hill is now worth 10 firsts,

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.500
then no one on planet Earth can afford you.

00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:49.625
- I appreciate your time.

00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:53.750
- [Goff:] And just like that, the QB market crashed overnight,

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.625
which produced…pure chaos.

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.000
- NO TEAM IS BETTER THAN SOME TEAMS!

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.541
- Protect me, uh...uh…Hurts...or Wentz, or Wentz...uh, um…or Hurts. Or Wentz.

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:06.000
- It’s gonna be good to get back—

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.875
Man, I hate this f--king sport.

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.500
- I need to figure out a way to cover this up.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.041
- Did somebody say "cover-up"?

00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:13.375
- [Roger Goodell:] URBAN MEYER!

00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:16.000
- Introducing: young kids you don’t need to pay.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.041
- WOAH, WHAT?!

00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:26.083
- Thank you all so much for watching this season.
It’s a real shame it has to end.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.500
You know what...I'm not leaving.

00:02:29.791 --> 00:02:32.791
I’m not f--king leaving. THE SHOW GOES ON!
WOOO! 

00:02:32.791 --> 00:02:34.541
- Clammy no. The season actually is over—

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:39.333
- THEY CAN NEVER SILENCE ME AS LONG AS YOU ALL 
BUY DELAWARE CLAMS SHIRTS IN THE 
BLEACHER REPORT STORE.

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:41.625
- Alright, the clam is belligerent. Send in Teamy.

00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:43.625
- SHIRTS SHOULD BE ABOUT TEAMY. 

00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:45.041
- COME AT ME, YOU F--KING PIECE OF S--T.

